{"base_rate":0.16005873715124816,"brier":0.09639309838472836,"bss":0.28300250689677287,"bss_hi":0.39432502291081856,"bss_lo":0.13132631621659627,"chart":{"base":[200.4,168.1],"fp":[233.9,131.0],"lead":"62,249.1 272,238.7 482,226 692,208.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.28 — higher than 51% of cities","fp":"low end +1pp, high end +27pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 47% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 0%; promised 79% → rained 54%"},"rel":"63,464.9 195.2,362.1 559,234.8"},"country":"NE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.061218795888399395,"ess":366.08018972800807,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Niamey</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Niamey rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (96%), believe about\n<b>67%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 681 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 8.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.28, ranked 106 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(56&ndash;167) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>406</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'><b>30%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>63%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Niamey</b> <span class=\"muted\">Niger</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;16% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 16% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.28</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>56&ndash;167\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>681 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Niamey &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Niamey\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.540591133004924,380.2068965517241 97.20417910447762,311.3731343283582 169.08090909090907,233.0909090909091 281.3594520547945,112.7397260273973 396.4034782608695,18.0 396.4034782608695,54.92753623188406 281.3594520547945,187.65890410958903 169.08090909090907,304.78787878787875 97.20417910447762,365.7014925373134 58.540591133004924,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"323.7386196769457\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"323.7386196769457\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.540591133004924,381.1034482758621 97.20417910447762,316.80597014925377 169.08090909090907,271.6969696969697 281.3594520547945,232.4109589041096 396.4034782608695,139.33333333333334\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 406 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.540591133004924\" cy=\"381.1034482758621\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"97.20417910447762\" cy=\"316.80597014925377\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 31%&amp;#10;It rained 30% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"169.08090909090907\" cy=\"271.6969696969697\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 63%&amp;#10;It rained 41% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"281.3594520547945\" cy=\"232.4109589041096\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 67% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"396.4034782608695\" cy=\"139.33333333333334\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(16%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Niamey the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.39) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (-0.19).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>155</td><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'>-0.192</td><td class='num'>2.5%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'>-0.069</td><td class='num'>18.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'>0.392</td><td class='num'>5.6%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>169</td><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'>nan</td><td class='num'>0.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":13.51366,"lon":2.1098,"n":681,"n_cities":216,"name":"Niamey","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0015270935960591135,"n":406,"obs":0.0024630541871921183,"sig":false},{"hi":0.22,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.11074626865671641,"n":67,"obs":0.1791044776119403,"sig":false},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.22,"mean":0.3137878787878787,"n":66,"obs":0.30303030303030304,"sig":false},{"hi":0.84,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.630958904109589,"n":73,"obs":0.410958904109589,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.84,"mean":0.9559420289855072,"n":69,"obs":0.6666666666666666,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":8.7,"provisional":false,"rank":106,"rank_hi":167.02499999999998,"rank_lo":56.0,"reliability":0.014138341222777519,"resolution":0.049576144326879325,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"niamey","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Niamey"}